PVD("afghanistan_ndp_2017-2021",{"docs":["","Afghanistan Vision Doc","AFG ANPDF 2017 2021"],"s":{"1":[[1,"24","5","Municipal Revenue Authority and Capacity Reform","Reforms should immediately focus on ensuring that municipal authorities have the authority and capacity to raise and manage revenues to deliver vital urban infrastructure and services.",""],[1,"24","5","Urban Land Access and Secure Property Rights Reform","Ensuring that urban arrivals can access land and establish secure land property rights is also vital for realizing potential economic and social benefits of an increasingly urban population.",""],[1,"51","16","Land Acquisition Law Reform","Approve land acquisition laws to formalize improved right of way and resettlement frameworks",""]],"2":[[1,"6","1","Public Expenditure Efficiency Improvement","Improve efficiency of public expenditure.",""],[1,"6","2","Reallocate Public Expenditures Toward High-Impact Activities","Move expenditures towards activities that have the greatest economic impact",""],[1,"6","3","Budget Process Strengthening and Resource Reallocation","Strengthen the budget process to free up fiscal space and reallocate resources towards growth priorities.",""],[1,"6","6","Policy Reform Commitment","Demonstrate commitment to policy reforms to build credibility.",""],[1,"6","8","Public Sector Institutional Reform Prioritization","Prioritize limited political capacity towards reforming the public sector institutions that matter most for growth.",""],[1,"7","9","Public Resource Allocation Improvement","Immediate improvements in public resource allocation and business environment reform can help escape slowdown.",""],[1,"25","1","Public Resource Allocation Improvement","Immediate improvements in public resource allocation and business environment reform can help escape slowdown.",""],[1,"33","12","Prioritization of Government Capacity and Political Capital","Prioritize scarce government capacity and political capital to address the institutional weaknesses that matter most.",""],[1,"69","3","Public Financial Management Reform and Anti-Corruption Measures","Donors may require changes or improvements to public financial management systems, including procurement and payroll systems or the implementation of anti- corruption measures before increasing on-budget support.",""],[2,"6","3","Budget Reform and Performance Improvement Framework","A credible national budget with the ability to improve government performance is the key mechanism for turning policy into tangible outcomes.",""],[2,"6","6","Governance, Anti-Corruption, and Organizational Reform Agenda","Improved governance, anti-corruption, and organizational reforms are woven into every section of this document.",""]],"3":[[2,"17","3","State Capacity-Building Investment for Reform Management","We will start by investing in human resources, administration, finance, IT and communications.","Ministry of Finance"],[2,"19","1","Public Sector Reform Continuation","Institutionalizing public sector reforms will continue over the life of the current administration.",""],[2,"19","1","Performance Management Reform for Revenue and Spending Ministries","Performance management reform will be introduced to the large revenue and spending ministries over the next three years.",""],[2,"19","1","Civil Service and Public Administration Reform","Civil service and public administration reforms are also being implemented to improve the quality of senior managers.",""],[2,"19","2","Civil Service Reform for Professionalization and Gender Balance","Afghanistan must establish a civil service that is responsive to national development needs and promotes the balanced participation of Afghan men and women.",""],[2,"19","4","Civil Service Legal Reform","Reforming the civil service by revising existing laws and enacting new ones, including changes to the Civil Servants Law;",""],[2,"19","6","Performance-Based Management Expansion","Expanding the use of performance-based management;",""],[2,"19","9","Performance Reward and Discipline Guidelines","Establishing guidelines to reward excellence and discipline under-performance.",""],[2,"44","10","Public Sector Capacity and Governance Reform Package","Professionally staffed and managed ministries, consolidated budget and PFM reform process, capable provincial and municipal subnational governments, electoral reform, citizen identity register",""],[2,"44","16","Civil Service Reform and Management Systems Rollout","This council will concentrate on reforms to the civil service, including devising appropriate rule and regulations; ensuring nationwide rollout of civil service management systems.",""],[2,"44","16","Civil Service Complaints Processing System","establish a transparent system to process complaints made by members of the civil service",""],[2,"44","16","CCR Capacity Building for Results Program","the implementation of the CCR Capacity Building for Results (CBR) program",""]],"4":[[2,"20","16","National Drug Action Plan","Since 2015, we have been implementing a National Drug Action Plan that aligns law enforcement, education, and public health.",""],[2,"20","16","Alternative Livelihoods for Farmers","over the next five years, we will continue to provide alternative livelihoods for farmers while strictly enforcing laws against money-laundering and drug trafficking.",""]],"5":[[1,"6","18","Coherent Growth Strategy Resource Alignment","Align all available resources around a coherent growth strategy.",""],[1,"6","19","Coherent Growth Strategy Alignment of Planning Processes","Align planning processes around a coherent growth strategy so that limited available resources have greatest possible impact",""],[1,"70","1","Strengthen Budget Planning and Prioritization","the effectiveness of the budget as a planning tool must be strengthened.",""],[1,"70","3","Sector Investment Plan Development","Develop costed and coherent sector investment plans linked to the ANPDF",""],[1,"70","4","Project Selection Criteria Development and Application","Develop and apply project selection criteria that reflect priorities within these plans",""],[2,"8","4","Sustainable Budget Transition and Long-Term Development Foundations","In the short-term, moving towards a sustainable budget and putting in place the foundations for Afghanistan's long-term development are our most important priorities.",""]],"6":[[1,"37","5","Citizen's Charter Program","The Citizen's Charter supports the Government's long-term goals of reducing poverty and deepening the relationship between citizens and the state.",""],[1,"37","6","Community Development Council Service and Grant Delivery","First, by providing development services and grants through CDCs, the government will increase trust that government can provide valued local benefits, deepening the social contract and improving perceptions of government.",""],[1,"37","6","Government-Citizen Charter Linkage","The Charter will help connect government, especially local government and municipalities, with its citizens.",""],[1,"37","7","Community Oversight for Service Delivery Accountability Program","by using community oversight over service provision through a high profile government program, the program will strengthen bottom-up accountability for service delivery and provide information to political leaders regarding service delivery successes and constraints.",""],[1,"51","6","Civil Society Cooperation for Transparency and Accountability","Close, strategic cooperation with civil society groups to strengthen transparency and accountability",""]],"7":[[2,"21","11","Human Rights Protection and Violence Against Women Prevention Measures","Taking serious steps to protect human rights and tackle violence against women.",""],[2,"31","13","Implementation of Human Rights and Protection Commitments for Afghan Women","Implementing our global commitments on human rights, security, and freedom from domestic violence for Afghan women;",""],[2,"31","16","Women’s Constitutional Rights Enforcement","Securing the constitutional rights for women through the full execution of our laws;",""]],"8":[[2,"5","1","Anti-Corruption and Justice Sector Reform","We will establish the rule of law and put an end to corruption, criminality, and violence.",""],[2,"5","1","Court Reform and Access to Constitutional Rights","Justice and the rule of law require that we step up the fight against corruption, reform our courts, and make sure that ordinary citizens can exert their constitutional rights with confidence.",""],[2,"20","5","Specialized Support to the Anti-Corruption Justice Centre","Providing specialized support to the Anti-Corruption Justice Centre to investigate and prosecute high-level corruption;",""],[2,"20","6","Prosecutor and Judge Entry and Refresher Examination Requirements","Introducing requirements for prosecutors and judges to pass entry and refresher exams,",""],[2,"20","17","Justice System Trust and Rule of Law Reform","First, citizens must come to trust the justice system and believe that their government will neutrally apply the rule of law to disputes.",""],[2,"21","1","Rule of Law System Reform Plans","The Supreme Court and the Attorney General's Office are producing reform plans to professionalize services and provide legal access to all citizens.",""],[2,"21","2","Judicial and Law Enforcement System Reform","Afghanistan will build a fair and just judicial and law enforcement system.",""],[2,"21","5","Transparent and Impartial Legal System Reform","Establishing a transparent and impartial legal system that is built around the rigorous application of the Constitution and international conventions on human rights;",""],[2,"21","6","Law Enforcement Professional Capacity Enhancement","Enhancing the professional capacity of law enforcement personnel at all levels;",""],[2,"21","7","Increase Women's Representation in Justice and Law Enforcement Agencies","Increasing the number of women in justice and law enforcement agencies;",""],[2,"21","8","Justice and Law Enforcement Coordination Improvement","Improving coordination between justice and law enforcement agencies;",""],[2,"21","9","Transfer of Land Management Adjudication to ARAZI","Transferring land management issues from the Supreme Court to ARAZI for professional adjudication;",""],[2,"21","10","Judicial Institutional Restructuring and Electronic Case Management System","Enhancing efficiency and responsiveness by restructuring judicial institutions and implementing an electronic case management system;",""],[2,"44","14","Court Presence Expansion and Case Management Modernization","Extending court presence to all provinces, justice ministry restructuring, expanding citizen access to the court, and information technology to improve case handling.",""]],"10":[[1,"6","4","Investor Confidence Support Measures","Support increased investor confidence.",""],[1,"6","5","Removal of Unnecessary Regulatory Constraints to Investment","Continue to remove unnecessary regulatory constraints to investment",""],[1,"16","1","Investment Promotion and Institutional Strengthening Reforms","The National Unity Government (NUG) has pursued a number of key reforms to boost investment and strengthen institutions.",""],[1,"16","5","Business Environment Reform and One-Stop Construction Permit Service","Business environment reforms have been progressed, including a one-stop shop for issuance of construction permits.",""],[1,"27","5","Business Environment Constraint Identification and Security Cooperation Measures","Working with business groups to identify possible measures to address binding business environment constraints, including cooperative arrangements for security",""],[1,"27","6","Investment Climate Reform to Reduce Business Costs","Implementing investment climate reforms to reduce the cost of doing business",""],[1,"28","1","Private Sector Investment Mobilization","Mobilizing growth sectors will require private sector investment.",""],[1,"29","1","National Priority Program for Private Sector Development","Government is currently in the process of developing a National Priority Program for Private Sector Development.",""],[1,"29","4","Business Ombudsman and Start-up Streamlining Reform","Appoint an ombudsman to help firms facing corruption at government agencies · Streamline business start-up processes and reduce fees",""],[1,"29","13","Foreign Investment Approval Process Streamlining","Streamline the foreign investment approval process",""],[2,"23","12","Private Sector Enabling Environment Reform","We will reduce red tape, clarify property titles, facilitate exports, provide reliable supplies of electricity, facilitate access to transport, and ensure the personal safety of entrepreneurs and businesspeople.",""],[2,"23","14","Business Process and Service Delivery Simplification Reform","We are committed to reforming business processes and plan to simplify administrative and service delivery procedures in major line ministries.","major line ministries"],[2,"23","14","One-Stop Shop Registration System","These rigorous initiatives include one-stop shops that consolidate dispersed services into a single location to speed up registration by orders of magnitude.",""],[2,"23","14","E-Administration Reform Package","These efforts will be complemented with selected e-administration reforms that will improve efficiency.",""],[2,"26","4","Investment Promotion","Encouraging domestic and international investment.",""],[2,"26","15","Licensing Requirement Simplification Reform","Reviewing licensing requirements with the goal of eliminating unnecessary ones;",""],[2,"26","16","Investment Tax Incentives and Legal Protection Framework","Providing tax incentives and legal protections of investments and assets to investors;",""],[2,"26","17","One-Stop Electronic Business Administration Services","Establishing one-stop shops offering streamlined electronic business administration services (registration, licensing, customs payments) in Kabul and seven hubs.",""],[2,"42","3","Private Sector Dialogue Mechanism","Dialogue with our private sector continues to improve.",""]],"11":[[1,"29","8","Serviced Industrial Park Land Identification","Identify land under ownership of defunct SOEs which can be used for serviced industrial parks",""],[1,"29","10","Pilot Special Economic Zone Development","Pilot Special Economic Zone (SEZ) development",""],[1,"29","10","Industrial Parks and SEZ Infrastructure Master Plan","Develop an infrastructure master plan for industrial parks, SEZs, and connective infrastructure.",""],[1,"29","14","State-Owned Enterprise Rationalization and Governance Improvement","Wind down moribund state-owned enterprises while improving governance and performance of those that are viable and serving a public purpose",""],[2,"18","7","Infrastructure Investment and Enabling Policy Reform for Job Creation","Investments in infrastructure and enabling policy reforms that can help the private sector create jobs must now replace them.",""],[2,"26","14","Industrial Parks and Special Economic Zones Development","Supporting and building industrial parks and special economic zones;",""]],"12":[[1,"52","10","MoMP Capacity Strengthening and License Oversight Support","Invest in and concentrate required capacity in MoMP.","MoMP"],[1,"52","10","International License Management Support","Meanwhile pull in international service providers to oversee and manage licenses.",""],[1,"64","7","Resource Corridor Approach for Extractive Sector Integration","Pursuing the resource-corridor approach to ensure that extractive activities are fully integrated into the broader economy, and benefits are relatively equitably shared.",""],[1,"64","8","Fiscal Framework for Mining Revenue Management","Ensuring that an appropriate fiscal framework is in place to smooth utilization of mining revenues and support long-term sustainable gains from extractives-financed programs and investments.",""],[1,"64","9","Incremental Proof-of-Concept Investment Diversification Approach","Utilizing an incremental, proof-of-concept approach to build a diversified portfolio of investments.",""],[1,"64","10","Institutional Responsibility and Capacity-Building for Mining Governance","Establishing clear institutional responsibilities and building required capacities in the Ministry of Mines and Petroleum and other involved government agencies, and accessing sustained international support for technically-demanding tasks.","Ministry of Mines and Petroleum"],[2,"26","26","Transparent Tendering and Monitoring for Extractive Industries","Their sustainable development through transparent tendering and effective monitoring is of particular importance to us.",""],[2,"26","26","EITI Compliance for Extractives Development","our strategic plans call for aligning extractives development with full EITI compliance",""],[2,"26","26","Heritage Site Conservation Standards for Extractive Activities","ensuring that activities in and around Afghanistan's heritage sites adhere to global best practices for conservation.",""],[2,"26","26","Opening Mining to International Investors","we will open up mining to international investors who can provide the capital and management skills needed to help this sector realize its full potential.",""],[2,"27","1","Mining Sector Legislative and Regulatory Reform","We will accelerate progress on the legislative and regulatory framework to encourage private sector investment.",""],[2,"27","2","Beneficial Ownership Disclosure and Revenue Collection Requirements","We will introduce new requirements for the disclosure of beneficial ownership and ensure that revenues from licensed exploitation are collected.",""],[2,"27","7","Illegal Mining Control Measures","Addressing illegal mining.",""],[2,"27","9","Contracting Reform and Internal Governance Professionalization","Reforming contracting and professionalizing internal governance;",""],[2,"27","10","Government Control over Mining Areas","Establishing full government control over mining areas;",""],[2,"27","11","Mining Law EITI Compliance Reform","Making the mining law EITI compliant;",""]],"14":[[1,"6","15","Agricultural Investment for Poverty Reduction and Job Creation","Invest in agriculture to reduce poverty, generate jobs, and improve livelihoods",""],[1,"64","12","Agricultural Productivity Improvement","Improved agricultural productivity and implementation of an improved social protection system could protect against such shocks.",""]],"15":[[1,"44","10","Irrigation Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Expansion","Rehabilitate and expand irrigation structures.",""],[1,"44","11","Water Management Improvement","Improve water management.",""],[1,"44","12","Land Management Systems and Capacity Investment","Invest in land management systems and capacity.",""],[2,"22","1","Support Programs for Labor-Intensive Agricultural Cash Crops and Processed Goods","We must adopt pro-active policies and support programs, particularly for labor-intensive agricultural cash crops and processed goods.",""],[2,"22","7","Farmland Demining Support","Continued support to de-mine farmland will return fertile land to farmers and reduce the risk of landmine injuries and fatalities in poor communities across Afghanistan.",""],[2,"22","8","Multi-Sectoral Agricultural Productivity Investment Programme","Increasing agricultural productivity requires significant multi-sectoral investments in irrigation resources, water management, improved planting materials, and best practices.",""],[2,"22","8","Agricultural Value Chain Development Initiative","Value chains must be developed to provide producers with greater incentives to invest.",""],[2,"22","8","Wheat and Cereal Production Expansion Programme","Increased wheat and cereal production, and expanding the depleted livestock herd, will provide food security for the country.",""],[2,"22","8","Urban-Rural Agricultural Linkages Improvement Initiative","Improved urban-rural linkages that provide inputs to buy, process and store farm products will lead to enhanced urban and transformative rural development.",""],[2,"23","5","Water Management Investment and Irrigation Rehabilitation Programme","Increasing investments in water management, with rehabilitation of more than 1,000 irrigation schemes, developing new irrigation networks and building small water reservoirs;",""],[2,"23","6","National Wheat Program","Implementing the national wheat program to increase yields to 26%, adding 110,000 hectares of land under cultivation, halving post-harvest losses, and developing a standardized wheat seed market;",""],[2,"23","7","Livestock Management and Import Protection Measures","Improving livestock management, applying phytosanitary entry criteria and WTO-allowed tariffs to prevent subsidized imports from competing with our smallholders;",""],[2,"23","8","Horticulture Capacity Expansion and Value Chain Support","Increasing horticulture capacity from 180,000 to 230,000 hectares, supporting investments in value-chains, establishing export certification procedures, and increasing support to women-owned agri-businesses;",""],[2,"23","9","Strategic Grain Reserve Rehabilitation and Grain Reserve Board Establishment","Rehabilitating the strategic grain reserve and establishing a Grain Reserve Board to support farmers;",""]],"16":[[2,"23","10","Agroforestry and Reforestation Expansion","Expanding agroforestry and reforestation with over 60,000 hectares that support environmental conservation and income generation for farmers;",""]],"17":[[2,"23","11","Ministry of Agriculture Decentralization and Reform","Restructuring the Ministry of Agriculture to become a decentralized and farmer-centric institution that regulates and encourages private investments.","Ministry of Agriculture"]],"19":[[1,"53","6","Regional Energy Connectivity Projects","Major regional energy projects are already underway and will help build regional connectivity in this area.",""],[1,"58","1","Distributed Electricity Generation Expansion","Distributed generation, including stand-alone and mini-grid systems, offer attractive options for extending electricity supply to the local population within the current context of uncertainty.",""],[1,"58","2","Distributed Electricity Access Expansion","This approach would reduce the need for risky and high-cost investments in large-scale grid-connected generation and transmission projects while accelerating supply of electricity to a large portion of the currently unserved population - especially in areas remote from the grid.",""],[1,"58","2","Small-Scale Renewable Energy Deployment","Small scale renewable technologies, such as Solar Home System (SHS), would be ideally suited to distributed generation.",""],[1,"58","2","Mini-Grid Electrification Programme","Mini-grids are well suited to either micro-hydro, solar arrays, or a combination of either solar or wind supplemented by diesel.",""],[1,"58","2","Community-Level Small-Scale Energy Delivery","Small- scale investments would be robust to fragility, and could be delivered through the Citizens Charter or other community-level programs, potentially improving perceptions of the state.",""],[1,"58","4","Distributed Electricity Generation Investments","Under a distributed generation scenario, generation investments would include mid- sized hydro and thermal investments connected to the grid, as well as smaller isolated projects in areas where grid connection would be costly and/or technically challenging.",""],[2,"27","1","Mining Transport and Energy Infrastructure Investment","Significant investments in critical infrastructure, particularly in railroads linking major mining projects to port facilities, and an enhanced national energy grid are needed to help realize mining's potential.",""],[2,"27","15","Electricity Generation and Transmission Program","Afghanistan has launched a long-term program for electricity generation and transmission.",""],[2,"27","15","CASA-1000 Power Transmission Project","Projects such as CASA-1000 and the Turkmenistan 500 KV power line could eventually carry up to 4000 MW of power.",""],[2,"27","15","Turkmenistan 500 KV Power Line","Projects such as CASA-1000 and the Turkmenistan 500 KV power line could eventually carry up to 4000 MW of power.",""],[2,"27","15","TAPI Natural Gas Pipeline Project","The TAPI natural gas pipeline is making progress toward delivering gas from Turkmenistan to South Asia.",""],[2,"27","16","Domestic Power Generation Expansion Masterplan","Domestic power generation is on the rise, with a masterplan to produce 2,300 MW from internal sources within five years, including four large hydroelectric projects developed as public-private partnerships (PPPs) and 600MW from solar, wind, and natural gas, also through PPPs.",""],[2,"27","16","National Grid Investment and Renewable Energy Expansion","Priority will be to continue to invest in the national grid, which is a fundamental prerequisite for commercial or industrial development, while making increasing investments in renewables for residential and isolated areas.",""],[2,"28","3","500 kV National Grid Completion","Complete the 500kv national grid and become energy self-sufficient within 15 years;",""],[2,"28","6","Private Sector Infrastructure Development Promotion","Encourage private sector infrastructure development;",""],[2,"28","7","Government Land Provision for Strategic Infrastructure","Where possible, provide cleared government-owned land to accelerate strategically important infrastructure;",""],[2,"28","8","Innovative Procurement Reform","Consolidate design and adopt innovative procurement to reduce tender and completion times;",""],[2,"28","9","Infrastructure Engineers and Project Managers Training Programme","Train a cadre of infrastructure engineers and project managers;",""],[2,"28","10","Domestic Power Generation Expansion","Increase domestic generation to 2,300 MW, using natural gas, renewable energy, and hydro-electricity;",""],[2,"28","11","Domestic Renewable Energy Supply and Transmission Development","Develop domestic energy supplies and transmission, especially through renewables;",""],[2,"28","12","Pricing and Subsidy Regime Normalization","Normalize the pricing and subsidy regime.",""],[2,"28","23","Regional Energy Project Funding and Administrative Support","Ensure regional energy projects, including CASA 1000 and TAPI, receive funding and administrative support;",""],[2,"40","1","Energy and Infrastructure Investment","We anticipate significant investment in energy and infrastructure to provide an enabling environment for business investment and ensure sustained growth.",""],[2,"45","9","Three-Tier National Energy Investment Strategy","National energy plan proposes a three-tiered investment strategy focusing on energy supply, institutional development, and regional trade, partnerships, and climate change mitigation.",""],[2,"45","9","New Domestic Power Generation Expansion","Approx. 2,300 MW from new domestic generation.",""],[2,"45","9","Regional Energy Cooperation Projects","Int'l projects include CASA 1000, TAPI, TUTAP, oil and gas exploration",""]],"20":[[1,"58","4","Private Investment Mobilization for Large-Scale Export-Oriented Power Projects","Even as a distributed generation was being pursued, government could continue to solicit private investment in large-scale projects with potential for export.",""],[1,"58","4","Public Investment in Large-Scale Export-Oriented Projects","Public investment in large-scale export-oriented projects could also be pursued in the future once immediate public investments in agriculture and human capital begin to deliver growth and revenue returns, generating additional fiscal space.",""],[1,"75","5","TAPI and CASA-1000 Energy Corridor Projects","TAPI and CASA-1000 proceed.",""]],"21":[[1,"6","9","Fragility Risk Mitigation Policy Measures","Pursue policy measures that mitigate fragility-related risks facing households and firms.",""]],"22":[[1,"51","7","Infrastructure Link Development and Coordination","Build missing infrastructure links and influence ones being built",""],[1,"55","7","Transit Trade Infrastructure Investment Prioritization","A sensible approach to transit trade development would be based on careful prioritization of infrastructure investment: i) to resolve existing congestion at important trade points; ii) to meet emerging needs in productive sectors (agriculture and mining); and iii) in partnership with the private sector.",""],[1,"56","11","Road Infrastructure Improvement","Improve road infrastructure and quality in response to demand from domestic exporters.",""],[2,"5","1","Strategic Infrastructure, Human Capital, and Technology Investment","We will make strategic investments in infrastructure, human capital, quality service delivery, and technology; backed by a robust and well-regulated financial sector that can channel money to where it can best be spent.",""],[2,"26","8","Customs-to-Customs Cooperation Agreements","Advancing customs-to-customs agreements with neighboring countries;",""],[2,"26","11","Transport and Logistics Sector Strengthening","Strengthening the transport and logistics sector, including the implementation of the Customs Convention on International Transport of Goods Under Cover of TIR Carnets (TIR Convention);",""],[2,"27","13","Freight Rail Link Expansion to Regional Networks","Building new freight rail links to regional networks in Turkmenistan and Iran.",""],[2,"27","14","Road Construction Firm Pre-qualification Process","To avoid these issues in the future, we will commence a process of pre-qualifying certified firms to build roads.",""],[2,"27","14","Transport Authority Strengthening and Institutional Establishment","Work is underway to improve transportation authorities by establishing systems that would allow them to harmonize responses to the country's expanding transport needs.",""],[2,"28","13","Cross-Border Energy Transmission and Dry Port Investment","We have made initial investments in cross-border energy transmission and dry ports for long- distance trans-shipment.",""],[2,"28","14","Regional Transport and Energy Connectivity Investments","Innovative areas of regional cooperation will be investments in the Central Asian digital highway, regional energy projects to augment the ones discussed earlier, and regional railways and roads.",""],[2,"28","14","Afghanistan Railway Connectivity and Logistics Hub Masterplan","The Afghanistan Railway Authority has prepared a commercial freight and mineral-focused development masterplan for establishing a northern link to Central Asia, a southwestern link to Iran, and six logistics hubs to provide export access to each of Afghanistan's major regions, of which approximately 350 KMs is at a stage of advanced design.",""],[2,"28","21","Participation in Regional Connectivity Projects","Join regional projects such as One Belt, One Road (OBOR);",""],[2,"28","22","Public-Private Partnership and Private Sector Infrastructure Development","Encourage PPPs and private sector infrastructure development;",""]],"23":[[1,"6","16","Human Capital Investment Expansion","Increase investment in human capital so that future growth opportunities can be captured.",""],[1,"44","13","Knowledge Extension Services Improvement","Improve availability and quality of knowledge extension services.",""],[1,"44","14","Rural Literacy Programs","Provide literacy programs for rural populations to improve productivity and to support rural community mobilization",""],[1,"46","10","Traditional Apprenticeships in Skills Training Programs","Include traditional apprenticeships in skills training programs to reach the large number of youth.",""],[1,"48","10","Skills Training Reform with Traditional Apprenticeships","Reform skills training programs to include traditional apprenticeships for unskilled and semi-skilled youth.",""],[1,"62","4","Human Capital Investment Incentive Measures","Increase incentives for human capital investment.",""],[2,"18","8","Vocational Education Alignment with Market Demand","From early childhood development to linking vocational education to market demands, investments to ensure a healthy and educated population will be of particular importance.",""],[2,"29","1","Vocational and Post-Secondary Skills Reform","To anticipate future market needs, we will invest in vocational education, engineering, managerial skills, the service industry, and on reforms to make Afghan labor more flexible and responsive.",""],[2,"29","1","Regulatory Reform for Migrant and IDP Training Access","Returning migrants and IDPs could offer positive contributions, provided regulatory reforms allow them to join secondary and vocational training programs.",""],[2,"29","1","Post-Secondary Quality Assurance and Curriculum Reform","We will improve the quality assurance of post-secondary institutions using an outcomes- based education model, and by restructuring curriculum, assessment, and reporting practices in education to ensure quality of learning.",""],[2,"29","7","Vocational and Technical Education Expansion","Expand vocational and technical education, utilizing the German apprenticeship model;",""],[2,"29","8","Private Skills Academies Establishment","Promote the establishment of private skills academies;",""],[2,"45","16","Vocational Education and Training Programmes","National programs for health, education, vocational education, women's economic empowerment, pension reform, and social safety nets",""]],"24":[[1,"46","4","Community Mobilization for School Attendance","Mobilize community involvement to encourage attendance.",""],[1,"46","5","Female Teacher Recruitment Initiative","Actively recruit female teachers.",""],[1,"46","9","Early Childhood Education Financing Support","Seek budget allocations and donor support for early childhood education.",""],[1,"46","14","Increase Education Resource Allocation","Increase overall resource allocation to education.",""],[1,"46","15","Medium-Term Education Needs Planning","Prepare a medium-term needs plan, paying attention to regional disparities in inputs and outcomes, with special consideration given to the maintenance needs for new schools.",""],[1,"46","16","Alignment of On- and Off-Budget Expenditures with the Needs Plan","Align on- and off-budget expenditures around the needs plan.",""],[1,"48","9","Early Childhood Education, Skills and Literacy Investment","Invest in early childhood education, skills and literacy programs.",""],[1,"48","11","Female Education Promotion","Strengthen focus on female education to close the gender gap and reduce fertility.",""],[2,"18","8","Early Childhood Development and Education Investment","From early childhood development to linking vocational education to market demands, investments to ensure a healthy and educated population will be of particular importance.",""],[2,"30","14","Literacy Expansion in Remote Areas","Both ministries are preparing reform plans to address these challenges, including improvements to the basic package of health services and programs to increase literacy in remote areas.",""],[2,"45","16","National Education Programmes","National programs for health, education, vocational education, women's economic empowerment, pension reform, and social safety nets",""]],"25":[[1,"48","7","Increase Education and Health Spending Share","Increase spending on education and health spending from 33 percent to 50 percent of civilian spending to ensure increased access and improvements in quality.",""],[1,"48","8","Primary Healthcare Service Expansion","Expand primary healthcare services, prioritizing rural areas.",""],[2,"16","8","Expansion of Education and Health Service Delivery","Increase development budget expenditures by 10-15 percent each year as we expand delivery of education and health services in the medium-term;",""],[2,"29","6","Workforce Health Investment Programme","Improve workforce quality through investments in preventative and curative health.",""],[2,"29","14","Sustainable Health System Financing Model","Define a sustainable model for health system financing.",""],[2,"30","14","Basic Health and Education Services Financing","This focus will continue with financing already secured for basic health and education services through 2020.",""],[2,"30","14","Health and Education Quality Improvement Reform Plans","health and education must now focus on improving quality, not just expanding coverage.",""],[2,"30","14","Basic Health Services Package Improvement","Both ministries are preparing reform plans to address these challenges, including improvements to the basic package of health services and programs to increase literacy in remote areas.",""],[2,"31","4","Basic Package of Health Services","The Basic Package of Health Services, including mandated services at all clinics, minimum hours of operation, and basic staffing requirements.",""],[2,"40","1","Health and Education Spending for Population Needs","A significant share of any growth will be used to address the health and education needs of our growing population.",""],[2,"45","16","National Health Programmes","National programs for health, education, vocational education, women's economic empowerment, pension reform, and social safety nets",""]],"26":[[1,"6","10","Broad Cash Transfer Scheme","Introduce a broad cash-transfer scheme to help households mitigate the long-term costs of security and other shocks",""],[1,"36","2","Poverty-Targeted Cash Transfer Scheme","Investing in a regular and predictable poverty targeted cash transfer that would provide 20 percent of the basic food basket value to 10 percent of the Afghan population (about 350,000 households).",""],[1,"64","12","Improved Social Protection System","Improved agricultural productivity and implementation of an improved social protection system could protect against such shocks.",""],[2,"30","11","Poverty Reduction Investment and Skills Support Strategy","Our strategy for poverty reduction combines investments to improve growth and productivity with targeted programs to help the poor improve their skills and access opportunities.",""],[2,"30","11","Mainstreaming Support for Vulnerable Citizens","We are committed to tackling these challenges by ensuring that provisions for helping our most vulnerable citizens are mainstreamed into our activities.",""],[2,"31","19","Cash Transfer Management Agency for Social Protection Entitlements","To improve their efficiency and reduce corruption, the Ministry of Labor, Martyrs and the Disabled will establish an agency to manage cash transfers for pensions, disability, and other social protection entitlements.","Ministry of Labor, Martyrs and the Disabled"],[2,"45","16","Pension Reform","National programs for health, education, vocational education, women's economic empowerment, pension reform, and social safety nets",""],[2,"45","16","Social Safety Nets","National programs for health, education, vocational education, women's economic empowerment, pension reform, and social safety nets",""]],"27":[[2,"11","5","Reintegration and Durable Solutions for Displacement","Reintegration of returning refugees and migrants, and durable solutions to internal displacement, must be a central part of Afghanistan's development plans;",""],[2,"11","6","Mainstream Returnee and IDP Support into Development Programs","Interventions in favor of returning refugees, migrants and IDPs should be built into existing development programs and follow a \"whole of community\" approach that complements humanitarian assistance and early recovery support;",""]],"29":[[2,"30","6","Urban Infrastructure Development","Build urban infrastructure - principally transport and drainage;",""],[2,"30","8","Urban Neighborhood Upgrading and Affordable Housing Initiative","Upgrade urban neighborhoods, provide and enforce zoning rules, and promote affordable housing;",""],[2,"30","9","Land Tenure Security and Urban Services Improvement","Certify and secure land tenure rights, improve urban services to the poor, and increase access to employment;",""],[2,"30","10","Urban Economic Zones and Metropolitan Hinterland Integration","Promote mass economies, establish urban economic zones,and integrate urban hinterlands into metropolitan developmentplanning.",""]],"30":[[2,"18","9","National Administration Titling Program","The Afghanistan Independent Land Authority (ARAZI) is working to meet this challenge by developing the National Administration Titling program.",""],[2,"23","15","National Land Certification Program","We are offering incentives to the urban poor to invest in their houses and small businesses through a national program for land certification that provides tenure security in all large and medium-sized cities.",""],[2,"30","13","National Priority Program on Land Administration","A central pillar of our anti-poverty approach is ARAZI's planned National Priority Program on land administration.",""],[2,"30","13","Urban Land Certification Program","This NPP will incorporate ongoing multi-agency urban land certification programs that are providing legally recognized occupancy certificates to irregular urban settlements.",""],[2,"44","14","National Land Administration Program","A national program for land administration (ARAZI) is also included in this NPP",""]],"31":[[1,"6","20","On-budget Aid Alignment Initiative","Bring a greater share of aid on to the budget to ensure alignment with policy priorities and maximize the local economic impact",""],[2,"6","7","Carefully Calibrated Bridge Support","Carefully calibrated bridge support is needed to make the transition to sustainability a smooth glide rather than a series of fitful and disruptive shocks.",""],[2,"6","7","Sustained Reform Partnership Mechanism","Sustaining partnerships to embed reforms and follow them through to fruition are pre-conditions for success.",""],[2,"28","13","Cross-Border Trade Project and Policy Reform Package","Afghanistan's recent accession to the WTO will facilitate more cross-border projects and policy reforms to promote regional trade, provided sufficient financing can be identified.",""],[2,"28","13","Investment Mobilization with IMF, ADB, and World Bank","We are working with the IMF,ADB, and the World Bank to develop models that can attract not only global investments but also domestic and regional private sector financing.",""],[2,"28","15","Regional Climate Change Cooperation Engagement","We will also step up our engagement with neighboring partners, South Asia Co-operative Environment Programme (SACEP), and The International Centre for Integrated Mountain Development (ICIMOD), on cooperation to mitigate the adverse effects of climate change across the trans-Himalayan region.",""],[2,"28","25","Strengthen Embassies and Trade Missions","Strengthen our embassies and trade missions.",""],[2,"34","2","Budget Support Through the National Budget","Channeling donor funds through the national budget is not only a more efficient, cost-effective use of money than off-budget programming is, but supporting the Afghan budget process is a necessary step towards a successful donor exit strategy.",""],[2,"34","4","Expanded Use of National Systems for Funded Programs","But the biggest potential for using funds efficiently is to use national systems wherever possible.",""],[2,"34","4","Pay-for-Results On-Budget Financing","a problem that could be solved by increasing the use of pay-for-results on-budget financing.",""],[2,"34","7","Agreement on Preconditions for Expanding On-Budget Support","Agreement on the pre-conditions for expanding on-budget support, either directly or through the ARTF;",""],[2,"34","8","Financing Alignment Dialogue and Review Procedures","Improve dialogue and review procedures to ensure alignment of all financing with government priorities and regarding quality of preparation;",""],[2,"35","1","Direct Donor Financing Support for Priority Development Activities","The government will continue to support direct donor financing for human rights workers, press and media development, targeted programs for vulnerable groups, strategic private sector development initiatives and other activities critical for national development.",""],[2,"35","1","Capacity-Building Partnerships for Large Infrastructure Investments","There are also specialized investments, particularly in large infrastructure, where the Afghan government lacks technical or managerial expertise and would be better served by partnerships that can build capacity through hands-on guidance and oversight.",""],[2,"35","1","Budget Recording and Development Council Review of Off-Budget Support","financial information should be recorded on the budget as early as possible using standard budget categories and reviewed as part of Development Council work plans.",""],[2,"35","2","Civil Society Dialogue and Partnership Mechanism","Dialogue with CSOs will continue on issues of mutual concern such as protecting and optimizing the civil society's monitoring and advocacy functions, introducing innovations in service delivery, and resolving partnership issues such as the management of withholding taxes on behalf of the government and any interference or corruption in CSO registration.",""]],"32":[[1,"29","5","Online Business Registration","Implement online business registration",""],[1,"29","5","E-Payment System for Taxpayers","Introduce e-payment for all taxpayers",""],[1,"46","11","Education Sector Payroll Management Information System","Introduce electronic systems for managing and ensuring validity of education sector payroll.",""]],"33":[[1,"16","9","Citizens' Charter Community Service Standards Program","The \"Citizens' Charter\" program will provide guaranteed minimum service standards to participating communities, through Community Development Councils.",""],[1,"37","1","National Solidarity Program Community Grants","The National Solidarity Program has been operational in some 35,000 communities across Afghanistan over the past 14 years.",""],[1,"37","8","Minimum Service Standards Program","The program is structured around minimum service standards.",""],[2,"19","7","Citizens' Charter Service Delivery Improvement","Enhancing the effectiveness of service delivery through the Citizens' Charter;",""],[2,"30","15","Citizens' Charter National Priority Program","The Citizens' Charter National Priority Program will improve mechanisms for service delivery in education, health, basic rural infrastructure, and agriculture services.",""],[2,"31","1","Citizens' Charter Basic Services Delivery Program","The Citizens' Charter will ensure the delivery of a basic package of services for all communities by 2026.",""],[2,"31","2","Universal Clean Water Access and Water Point Provision","Universal access to clean water, providing nearly 20,000 water points;",""],[2,"31","6","Rural Renewable Electricity Access","Basic electricity from renewable sources in remote areas which cannot be reached by the grid system;",""],[2,"31","7","Basic All-Year Rural Roads","Basic all-year roads to increase village to market access;",""],[2,"31","18","Jobs for Peace Program","We will reduce poverty primarily by helping the poor increase their skills, productivity, and access labor- intensive paid employment through the Jobs for Peace program.",""]],"34":[[1,"6","21","Public Investment Management Strengthening","Strengthen public investment management processes to ensure all expenditure is of high quality and aligned with policy priorities.",""],[1,"16","6","Centralized Public Procurement Unit","A centralized procurement unit has been established to better control and safeguard expenditures.",""],[1,"70","5","Investment Management Capacity Concentration","Build and concentrate capacity for investment management within a small group of growth-relevant ministries",""],[1,"70","7","Public Investment Project Management Training Programme","Provide training and \"train the trainer\" programs on project selections, assessment, management, and monitoring to those agencies with key roles to play in managing public investments",""],[1,"70","8","Public Financial Management System Modernization","Continue to strengthen and modernize core government public financial management systems",""],[1,"70","9","Budget Process Improvement","Maintain progress with improving the budget process, strengthening procurement, building audit capacities, and reviewing alignment between public spending and policy priorities",""],[1,"70","9","Public Procurement Strengthening","Maintain progress with improving the budget process, strengthening procurement, building audit capacities, and reviewing alignment between public spending and policy priorities",""],[1,"70","9","Audit Capacity Building","Maintain progress with improving the budget process, strengthening procurement, building audit capacities, and reviewing alignment between public spending and policy priorities",""],[1,"70","9","Public Spending Alignment Review","Maintain progress with improving the budget process, strengthening procurement, building audit capacities, and reviewing alignment between public spending and policy priorities",""],[1,"70","10","Public Investment Management Strengthening","Strengthen public investment management processes from project selection to monitoring and evaluation",""],[2,"16","10","Budget Formulation, Execution, and Reporting Reform","we will undertake comprehensive reforms to the way the budget is formulated, executed and reported.",""],[2,"16","10","National Budget Consolidation Reform","Fixing Afghanistan's budgeting systems, including budget consolidation, requires deep, foundational reforms.",""],[2,"16","10","Project Filtering and Review Procedures","We will work with development partners and domestic constituents such as the Parliament to establish filtering and review procedures to improve project quality at inception and increase our flexibility to align resources to performance.",""],[2,"16","12","Consolidated National Budget","We will work towards a consolidated national budget by 2019;",""],[2,"16","13","Simplified Medium-Term Budget and Expenditure Framework","We will supplement the current medium-term fiscal framework with a simplified medium-term budget and expenditure framework that sets out the estimated cost of government policy over four years; and",""],[2,"16","14","Annual Budget Process Revision","We will revise the annual budget process in line with national priorities.",""],[2,"16","15","Public Finance Management Reform","We are reforming public finance management to improve national accountability systems.",""],[2,"17","1","National Priorities Statement for Budget Preparation","A statement of national priorities based on improved macroeconomic and fiscal analysis will guide the preparation of the annual budget.",""],[2,"17","1","Budget Submission Alignment to National Priorities","This will assist the Directorate General of Budget to direct budget submissions towards national priorities with a clear understanding of the fiscal space available for investments and national development priorities.",""],[2,"18","5","National Priority Programme Budget Allocation and Annual Performance Review","The national budget process will allocate resources to NPPs and review their performance annually.",""],[2,"22","2","Investment Allocation Framework for Growth and Social Sectors","The High Economic Council has approved a 70-30 split in investment between growth and social sectors.",""],[2,"22","4","Performance-Oriented Budget Allocation Reform","Our performance-oriented approach to budget management will ensure that those sectors that can show credible investment ideas, have a history of good performance and the governance reforms needed to bring them to fruition will receive larger shares of our scarce financial resources.",""],[2,"22","5","Sectoral Investment Pipeline for National Priority Programmes","Each prioritized sector will produce an investment pipeline aligned to outcomes proposed by the Cabinet and in line with available resources.",""],[2,"22","5","Annual NPP Investment Proposal and Budget Review Process","As part of the annual budget process, a detailed sectoral vision for each NPP, along with a ranked set of interventions, quantified outputs and a reviewed budget, will be included in investment proposals presented by each ministry to the Cabinet and the High Economic Council.",""],[2,"22","6","National Priority Programme Feasibility and Design Preparation","By starting the feasibility and design work now, we can gain a sense of required financial and organizational resources, provide a framework for sequencing, and set priorities based on informed assessments of costs.",""],[2,"26","13","Private Sector Survey Instrument Improvement and Systematization","Improving and systematizing private sector survey instruments;",""],[2,"26","21","State-Owned Bank Risk Monitoring Unit","Establishing a unit to monitor risks from state-owned banks;",""],[2,"26","23","DAB Safeguards Review Completion","Completing the DAB safeguards review by 2017;",""],[2,"34","2","Consolidated Budget-Based Policy Implementation","Afghanistan's reform agenda rests on the government ability to use a consolidated budget as the primary instrument for carrying out policy.",""],[2,"34","3","Structured Project Review System","The government needs a more structured project review system for its on-budget projects to weed out projects that lack precision.",""],[2,"34","17","PEFA Rating Update","Update Afghanistan's Public Expenditure and Financial Accountability (PEFA) rating, which is an internationally recognized instrument for assessing fiduciary risk.",""]],"35":[[1,"16","7","Revenue Policy and Administration Strengthening","Strengthen revenues.",""],[1,"19","3","Tax Administration Reform and VAT Introduction","The Government is working on further reforms to tax administration and plans to introduce a VAT in 2019.",""],[1,"72","1","Revenue Compliance and Policy Improvement","Continued efforts to improve revenue compliance and policy could help increase revenues over time.",""],[1,"72","1","Electronic Revenue Administration Systems Roll-out","Administrative improvements, including the roll-out of electronic systems, should be prioritized.",""],[2,"14","2","Annual Fiscal Strategy Paper","The Fiscal Strategy Paper, which will be approved by the High Economic Council and published annually, will outline progress made on reforms and provide the macroeconomic basis for forecasting revenues.",""],[2,"14","4","Concessional Borrowing Policy for Specific Projects","We will not borrow in the medium term, except on a concessional basis for specific projects.",""],[2,"15","1","Domestic Tax Base Strengthening","We need a strong domestic tax base to help support our move away from donor assistance",""],[2,"16","2","Fiscal Policy for Economic Management and Shock Insulation","We will use fiscal policy as the primary tool for economic management; both to invest in the economy and, where possible, to insulate it from shocks;",""],[2,"16","3","Domestic Revenue Mobilization for Development Financing","We will over time collect enough revenue to meet operational and more of our development needs, gradually reducing development assistance over the next fifteen years;",""],[2,"16","4","Fiscal Balance and Concessional Borrowing Policy","We will balance the budget over the medium to long-term, without borrowing unsustainably.",""],[2,"17","1","Macroeconomic and Fiscal Performance Department","The newly established Macroeconomic and Fiscal Performance Department (MFPD) will bring revenue and expenditure estimates together and present the fiscal outlook to the Cabinet.",""],[2,"17","2","Budget Transparency and Forecasting Reform","A range of measures to ensure that the budget is accurate, transparent and robust will reinforce this improvement in the policy setting process.",""],[2,"38","4","Macroeconomic Stabilization Continuation","Progress will continue on macroeconomic stabilization to minimize the risk of shocks;",""],[2,"38","5","Domestic Revenue Mobilization and Transit and Mining Revenue Framework","Domestic revenue collection will increase in line with nominal GDP, which is projected to be 5 percent on average per year until 2020.",""],[2,"38","5","Legal and Regulatory Frameworks for Transit and Mining Revenue Realization","Once legal and regulatory frameworks are in place, revenues from transit and major mining projects will be realized by 2020 and beyond;",""]],"36":[[1,"6","11","Regulatory Simplification and Financial Access Support","Reduce unnecessary regulatory constraints, improve access to financial services, and introduce new financial instruments to help firms better deal with insecurity.",""],[1,"29","7","Financial Inclusion Strategy Finalization","Finalize the Financial Inclusion Strategy",""],[1,"29","9","Islamic Banking Legal and Regulatory Reform","Remove legal and regulatory constraints to Islamic banking",""],[1,"40","3","Insurance Industry Development and Deposit Insurance Strengthening","This will require development of a well-regulated insurance industry and an increase in savings rates through expanding financial inclusion, including trust-building through strengthened deposit insurance.",""],[1,"40","3","Financial Inclusion Expansion","This will require development of a well-regulated insurance industry and an increase in savings rates through expanding financial inclusion, including trust-building through strengthened deposit insurance.",""],[1,"40","3","Banking Sector Expansion for Social Protection Support","Financial sector development and expansion of the banking sector would also help with the development of social protection mechanisms.",""],[2,"23","15","Mobile Banking and E-Payment Expansion","In the future, mobile banking and e-payment facilities will reduce transaction and interest costs for poor or isolated communities otherwise excluded from the financial system.",""],[2,"26","18","Financial Sector Reform Strategy","We have a two-pronged strategy for financial sector reform.",""],[2,"26","19","Financial Sector Regulatory and Monitoring Framework Strengthening","Enhancing regulatory and monitoring frameworks to bring stability to the financial sector;",""],[2,"26","20","Risk-Based Audit and Review Model Expansion","Increasing the use of risk-based audit and review models;",""],[2,"26","22","Oversight Regulation Review and Rationalization","Reviewing oversight regulations to eliminate duplication and make sure that they are fit for purpose;",""],[2,"26","24","Private Bank Lending Incentive Scheme","Providing incentives for private banks to lend to private enterprises;",""],[2,"26","25","National Financial Inclusion Strategy","Preparing a national financial inclusion strategy, to allow citizens better access to banking services, by December 2017.",""]],"37":[[1,"29","16","Coordinated Implementation Action Plan for Trade Strategies and Policies","Develop an action plan for coordinated implementation of existing trade-related strategies and policies",""],[1,"29","20","Expansion of the One-Stop Export Shop for Air-Freight Exports","Expand the operations of the one-stop export shop to include air-freight exports",""],[1,"56","4","Agricultural Export Development","By and large, employment impacts will be maximized through the development of agriculture exports.",""],[1,"56","13","Regional Trade Agreement Expansion","Deepen and expand existing trade agreements with regional partners.",""],[2,"9","10","Regulatory and Operational Barrier Reduction for Investment and Exports","We will reduce regulatory and operational barriers to investments and exports to facilitate this expansion.",""],[2,"22","1","Regional Integration and Governance Reform Agenda","To build a competitive economy, Afghanistan needs to advance regional integration, improve governance, and transform its productive sectors to effect growth-inducing reforms and investments.",""],[2,"22","1","WTO-Allowed Trade Protection Procedures","WTO-allowed procedures should be used to prevent Afghan producers from being driven out of the market by cheaper imported products.",""],[2,"23","13","SME-Focused Policy for Import Substitution and Export Support","Our SME-focused policy will concentrate on satisfying local demand, promoting import-substitution in areas where Afghanistan should have a comparative advantage, supporting exports through access to credit and reducing red tape-driven obstacles.",""],[2,"26","6","ISO Standards Compliance Support for Afghan Firms","Assisting Afghan firms to comply with ISO standards;",""],[2,"26","9","Strengthening Commercial Attachés in Afghan Embassies","Strengthening commercial attachés in Afghan embassies;",""],[2,"26","10","Bilateral and Multilateral Trade Agreement Advancement","Advancing bilateral and multilateral trade agreements;",""],[2,"26","12","Local Procurement and Import Substitution Promotion","Promoting local procurement and allowable import substitution;",""]],"38":[[1,"29","19","Customs Reform Program","Implement the Customs Reform program and Trade Facilitation Agreement",""],[1,"56","9","Single Window and Trade Information Portal","Improve efficiency in documentation requirements and processes, including establishing a single window and information portal for trade.",""],[1,"56","10","Cross-Border Customs and Border Capacity Improvement","Improve cross-border institutions to reduce wait times at strategic border points by offering 24/7 customs services, reducing traffic congestion, and expanding border capacity.",""]],"39":[[1,"16","8","Regional Integration and Cross-Border Connectivity Cooperation","Support regional integration.",""],[2,"8","2","Promotion of Growth-Inducing Economic Cooperation with Neighbors","Afghanistan's geo-strategic location at the crossroads of one of the world's most dynamic and populous regions means that it is well positioned to foster growth-inducing economic cooperation with our neighbors.",""]],"40":[[1,"53","7","Promotion of Private Investment in Fibre-Optic Networks","the Government is working hard to promote private investment in fibber- optic networks including through participation in regional initiatives.",""]],"41":[[1,"27","2","Reorientation of Budget Expenditures Toward Labour-Intensive Community Programs","Reorienting budget expenditures towards labour-intensive and community-based programs that directly reach the population with the greatest needs and spur consumption, driving economy-wide benefits",""],[2,"29","3","Labor Market Preparation and Labor Export Promotion","Prepare for future labor market needs, including labor exports;",""],[2,"29","9","Migrant and Displaced Population Labor Market Integration Program","Identify opportunities to absorb returning migrants and displaced populations into training programs and labor markets;",""],[2,"29","10","Community-Based Income Generation Support for Persons with Disabilities","Support community-based approaches to income -generation for people with disabilities;",""],[2,"29","11","Labor Policy and Regulatory Review for Greater Flexibility","Review labor policy and regulations to increase flexibility;",""]],"42":[[2,"19","10","Presidential Anti-Corruption Action Plan","The presidential action plan for fighting corruption combines prevention with a strong program and sound leadership at the Supreme Court and Attorney General's Office that will end the culture of impunity and send the corrupt to justice.","Supreme Court | Attorney General's Office"],[2,"20","1","Institutional Anti-Corruption Reform Agenda","Combating Afghanistan's institutionalized corruption requires major reforms to its security, organizational, economic, and legal institutions.",""],[2,"20","2","Public Procurement Reform","Revamping public procurement, which accounts for 20% of total expenditure;",""],[2,"20","3","High Council on Rule of Law and Anti-Corruption","Establishing the High Council on Rule of Law and Anti-corruption;",""],[2,"20","4","Ministry-Level Anti-Corruption Action Plans","Producing ministry-level anti-corruption action plans, beginning with Finance, Mining and Petroleum, Commerce and Industry, Communication and Technology, and Transport;",""],[2,"20","8","Electronic Payments and E-Procurement Expansion","Increasing the use of electronic payments and e-procurement.",""],[2,"34","10","Audit and Accountability Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthened mechanisms for audit and accountability.",""],[2,"34","12","National Anti-Corruption Action Plan and Legal Framework","Implement the national anti-corruption action plan and legal framework;",""],[2,"34","13","Anti-Corruption Criminalization Legislation","Pass laws criminalizing corruption in line with the UN Convention Against Corruption;",""],[2,"34","14","Expanded Public Disclosure of Asset Declarations","Expand public disclosure of asset declarations to cover law enforcement, customs, and tax administration;",""],[2,"34","15","Electronic Payments and E-Procurement Expansion","Expand the use of electronic payments and e-procurement to line ministries;",""],[2,"34","16","Strengthening of the Supreme Audit Office","Strengthen the Supreme Audit Office;",""],[2,"42","3","Comprehensive Anti-Corruption and Legal System Reform","Comprehensive reforms are underway to reduce corruption and build a legal system that can enforce the law.",""]],"43":[[2,"20","9","Permanent Government Presence Expansion Program","An investment program to extend a permanent government presence to provinces and districts combined with increasing the share of spending through subnational governments and reforming the electoral process, including direct elections for mayors by 2019, will strengthen subnational governance.",""],[2,"20","9","Subnational Fiscal Decentralization Reform","An investment program to extend a permanent government presence to provinces and districts combined with increasing the share of spending through subnational governments and reforming the electoral process, including direct elections for mayors by 2019, will strengthen subnational governance.",""],[2,"20","9","Electoral Process Reform for Direct Mayoral Elections","An investment program to extend a permanent government presence to provinces and districts combined with increasing the share of spending through subnational governments and reforming the electoral process, including direct elections for mayors by 2019, will strengthen subnational governance.",""],[2,"20","13","Municipal Capacity Strengthening for Revenue Collection and Service Delivery","Strengthening municipal capacity for revenue collection and service delivery;",""],[2,"20","15","Provincial and District Governor Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of provincial and district governors.",""],[2,"20","17","Local Service Delivery and State Presence Initiative","Second, the state and its officials must develop a positive presence, largely around their ability to deliver locally valued services.",""],[2,"30","4","Decentralized Urban Planning and Participatory Urban Governance Mechanisms","Decentralizing urban planning and establishing participatory urban governance mechanisms.",""],[2,"30","5","Urban Governance and Rule of Law Reform","Improve the legal and regulatory framework, implement devolution of power, and strengthen the rule of law in cities;",""]],"44":[[2,"29","12","Women's Education and Market Employment Investment","Invest in women's education and market employment;",""],[2,"31","9","Women’s Political, Social, and Economic Participation Initiative","We are committed to ensuring the full political, social, and economic participation of Afghan women in national development.",""],[2,"31","10","Women's Economic Empowerment Program Investment","over the next fifteen years, we will invest as much as USD250 million in the women's economic empowerment program",""],[2,"31","10","Women's Mobility and Economic Access Reform Agenda","We will enact a reform agenda to increase women's mobility, improve the quality of gender statistics, and reduce or eliminate regulations that block women's access to credit and markets",""],[2,"31","15","Women's Economic Empowerment National Priority Program","Launching the Women's Economic Empowerment National Priority Program;",""],[2,"33","1","Women's Economic Empowerment Program","Over the next fifteen years, we will invest as much as USD250 million in the women's economic empowerment program",""],[2,"45","16","Women's Economic Empowerment Programmes","National programs for health, education, vocational education, women's economic empowerment, pension reform, and social safety nets",""]],"46":[[1,"16","3","Military Leadership and Governance Reform","Strengthen leadership and governance in the military.",""],[2,"6","4","National Security and Armed Services Professionalization Investment","As part of our national security strategy, we will continue to invest in professionalizing and increasing the effectiveness of the armed services.",""],[2,"9","1","National Campaign Plan for Security Force Mobility and Effectiveness","We have adopted a five-year National Campaign Plan to increase the mobility and effectiveness of our security forces.",""],[2,"9","1","Security, Reconciliation, and Stability Plan","The Plan focuses on three areas: reconciliation, security, and stability.",""],[2,"9","1","Military Leadership Reform and Officer Training Professionalization","We have revamped our senior military leadership and professionalized training for officers.",""]],"47":[[1,"29","3","Business-Led Security and Crime Prevention Cooperation","Facilitate collective approaches to security and crime-prevention between businesses",""],[2,"9","1","Security Force and Police Capacity Improvement","Improvements to the ANSF and the police are critical not only for securing our country against armed opposition groups but also for reducing criminality such as extortion, kidnapping, and illegal seizure, which have become huge disincentives to business investment.",""]],"48":[[1,"46","3","Border Security Boundary Wall Construction","Build boundary walls to improve security.",""],[2,"9","1","Landmine and Explosive Remnant Clearance","Presence of landmines and Explosive Remnant of War (ERW) pose a threat to the lives of Afghan civilians and impede development activities.",""]],"49":[[2,"9","1","Civilian Oversight of Security Support Functions","Civilian controls over principal support functions such as procurement, financial management, and audit have been introduced.",""],[2,"9","1","Anti-Corruption Measures for Force Effectiveness","We have introduced tough measures to end the internal threat to force effectiveness caused by corruption.",""],[2,"9","2","Domestic Revenue Mobilization for Security Sector Financing","we are committed to significantly improving domestic revenue collection",""],[2,"9","2","Security Sector Efficiency and Anti-Corruption Monitoring Mechanism","improving efficiencies through preventing corruption, misuse of funds and strict spending monitoring mechanisms in the security sector",""]],"50":[[1,"29","17","Review Afghanistan-Pakistan Transit Trade Agreement and Expand Transit Trade Coverage","Review the Afghanistan Pakistan Transit Trade Agreement and consider expanding to other countries",""],[1,"29","18","Improved Visa Arrangements Negotiation","Negotiate improved visa arrangements with UAE and other key partners",""],[1,"56","12","Pakistan Dialogue on APTTA Implementation Constraints","Continue discussions with Pakistan on resolving APTTA implementation constraints.",""]],"51":[[1,"6","14","Extractives Sector Development Initiative","Pursue extractives development to mobilize required revenues and foreign exchange receipts",""],[1,"19","3","Illegal Mining Regulation and Royalty Collection Enforcement","Regulating illegal mining and improving collection of royalties from licensed mines could also help, but this would require much stronger enforcement capacity.",""],[1,"52","8","Scalable Proof-of-Concept Investment Identification","Identify opportunities for scalable proof of concept investments.",""],[1,"52","9","Geodata Dissemination and Private Sector Outreach Initiative","Restore interest in exploration activities by disseminating geodata and improving outreach activities to private sector.",""],[1,"52","11","Resource Corridor Program Reenergization","Reenergize resource corridor program.",""],[1,"72","1","Mobilization of New Growth Sources Including Extractives","Further increasing revenue would require the mobilization of new sources of growth, including extractives.",""],[1,"75","6","Mining Sector Public and Private Investment Mobilization","Mining development proceeds with required public investments and efforts to attract private investment.",""],[1,"75","9","Additional Mining Investments","Additional mining investments (Aynak copper, Hajigak iron ore, medium-scale coal, marble, chromite, gold, lithium).",""],[2,"8","2","Modernization of Agriculture, Mining, and Inter-Regional Trade","But the old ways must be modernized.",""]],"52":[[1,"51","8","Integrated Power and Water Planning","Integrate power, water plans",""]],"53":[[1,"29","14","Skilled Foreign Staff Visa Facilitation in Investment Approval","Issue visas for skilled foreign staff as part of investment approval processes",""],[1,"42","10","Managed Labor Mobility Investment","investing in managed labor mobility can provide growth, income, and stability benefits.",""],[1,"61","4","Managed Migration Flows through Bilateral Labor Migration Agreements","Managed migration flows, based on bilateral labor migration agreements, promise improved regularity of migration patterns, access to higher-wage countries,",""],[1,"62","1","Economic Migrant Employment Expansion","Double current levels of economic migrants and offer additional job opportunities for 10,000 to 50,000 people annually, reducing fragility risks through the employment channel.",""],[1,"62","2","Immediate Wage Increase for Workers Placed Abroad","Immediate wage increases of 300 to 800 percent for workers placed abroad.",""],[1,"62","8","Labor Market Access Negotiation for Afghan Workers","Identify potential host countries and negotiate labor market access for Afghan workers.",""],[1,"62","9","Inter-governmental Coordination Mechanism for Visa and Exit Clearance","Create an inter-governmental coordination mechanism and streamline visa and exit clearance processes.",""],[1,"62","10","Labor Intermediation and Skills Certification System","Strengthen labor intermediation for Afghans going abroad by establishing systems for recruitment and skills certifications and verification.",""],[1,"62","11","Migrant Mobility Protection Support Measures","Balance mobility with protection by strengthening embassy services in host countries, offering pre- departure training, and conducting information campaigns.",""]],"54":[[2,"17","1","Policy Department Reinforcement for Councils Support","We have reinvigorated the Policy Department to support the Councils, whose primary function is to guide national development priorities.",""],[2,"17","1","Procedures for the Councils","This is a Cabinet Secretariat role, which focuses on establishing robust procedures for the Councils.",""],[2,"18","1","Cabinet-Policy-Budget Alignment Mechanism","Aligning the Cabinet, policy priorities, and the budget is at the heart of our national development strategy.",""],[2,"18","3","Inter-Ministerial Councils for Development Policy Coordination","Inter-ministerial Councils will set development priorities, oversee policymaking, eliminate fragmentation of mandates, monitor progress and facilitate measures for development in their respective sectors.",""],[2,"18","3","High Economic Council Economic Policy and Budget Forum","The High Economic Council serves as the umbrella forum for making final decisions on economic policy and budgetary allocations.",""],[2,"18","3","Inter-Ministerial Committee Policy Recommendation and Monitoring System","Inter-ministerial committees will make policy recommendations and monitor their implementation.",""],[2,"18","4","National Priority Programs Coordination and Budgeting Framework","Inter-ministerial working groups will synchronize timetables, budgets, and shared resources.",""],[2,"20","12","Budgeting, Planning, and Implementation Coordination Support","Improving support and coordination for budgeting, planning, and implementation;",""],[2,"34","18","Policy-to-Budget Dialogue Framework","Making the Afghan policy-to-budget process the centerpiece of the dialogue will guide both on and off-budget partnerships since the goal for both is to build up Afghan systems.",""]],"55":[[2,"20","17","Cultural Heritage and National Identity Initiative","Third, the country will use its rich cultural heritage to build a national identity and sense of citizenship that rises above local enmities and perceived differences.",""],[2,"21","12","Use of Historical and Cultural Resources for Pluralism","Governors, mayors, and other leaders will be encouraged to use historical and living cultural resources to advance pluralism.",""],[2,"21","12","Culture Mainstreaming in Planning Mechanism","The Trust Fund will be the mechanism through which we will work with civil society to incorporate culture into planning.",""],[2,"21","12","Pluralistic Citizenship Curriculum and Teacher Training","The school curriculum and teacher training programs must encourage the development of pluralistic citizenship in young people.",""],[2,"21","12","Domestic Tourism Development","The potential for domestic tourism has also been under-appreciated not only as an area for development but also as a means of overcoming the legacy of conflict.",""],[2,"30","7","Cultural Heritage Integration in Urban Development Plans","Integrate cultural heritage into urban development plans;",""]],"56":[[2,"27","2","Hydrocarbon Mapping and Exploration","Hydrocarbon mapping and exploration are also underway although any significant commercial development will have to await global price increases for oil and gas.",""],[2,"27","6","Oil and Gas Exploration Expansion","Expanding oil and gas exploration;",""]],"57":[[2,"14","5","Gradual Domestic Financing of Security Costs","The Government will gradually finance an increasing share of security costs.",""],[2,"42","3","Security Force Reform Programme","The reforms to our security forces are slowly reducing citizen insecurity and our country's vulnerability to attacks.",""],[2,"42","3","National Territory Control and Reconstruction Process","As we re-assert and sustain control over the whole of the national territory, the process of rebuilding can begin.",""]],"58":[[2,"42","3","Parliamentary and National Election Planning","Planning for parliamentary and national elections is advancing.",""]]}});